.TH GRABIT 1 "2026-07-20" "grabit 0.5.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
grabit \- screenshot, recording, OCR, and upload for Wayland compositors
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B grabit
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B grabit
.BR set | get | unset
.RI [ key "] [" value ]
.br
.B grabit
.B sxcu
.RB { add | list | show | remove }
.RI [ arg ]
.br
.B grabit
.B plugin
.RB { install | list | show | update | remove }
.RI [ arg ]
.br
.B grabit
.B help
.RI [ subcommand ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B grabit
captures region screenshots, records the screen, performs OCR, and uploads the
result, with a native freeze + region selector. It uses
.B zwlr_screencopy_v1
when advertised, otherwise
.BR ext_image_copy_capture_v1 ,
otherwise the
.B org.kde.KWin.ScreenShot2
dbus service on KDE Plasma.
.PP
Supported compositors: Hyprland, sway, niri, river. KDE Plasma works for
screenshots only: KWin implements neither capture protocol, and its ScreenShot2
service is single-shot, so
.B \-\-record
is unavailable there. X11 and GNOME are not supported.
.PP
With no action flag, grabit performs the configured
.B default_action
(seeded to
.B copy
on first run, which also writes a default config to
.IR ~/.config/grabit/config.toml ).
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-copy
Copy the screenshot to the clipboard.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-upload
Upload the screenshot to the default service (the
.B service
config key). On success the resulting URL is copied to the clipboard and
printed to standard output. Uploaded recordings do the same.
.TP
.BI \-\- service
Upload to a specific built-in service
.RB ( zipline ,
.BR nest ,
.BR fakecrime ,
.BR ez ,
.BR guns ,
.BR pixelvault )
or a registered
.B .sxcu
uploader.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output ", " \-\-save
Capture, save to disk, and print the path to standard output. The \(dqSaved\(dq
notification and shutter sound are emitted only when standard output is a
terminal, so redirecting the path to a file or pipe is silent by design.
.TP
.B \-\-record
Toggle screen recording (run again to stop). Records a region to MP4/H.264
(or WebM/GIF via
.BR "grabit set recording.format webm|gif" )
with a live border overlay, an on-screen control bar, and an SNI tray icon.
The bar opens at the top of the current monitor (falling back to a spot that
stays out of the recording) and offers start (resume), pause, and stop, plus
a state dot and an elapsed timer; drag it by its background to move it.
Pausing closes the current encoder segment and resuming opens a new one; on
stop the segments are stitched together, so paused time is cut from the
output rather than left as a frozen gap. Sending
.B SIGUSR1
to the recording process also toggles pause (for compositor keybinds). After
stopping, a "Recording finishing" notification is shown while encoders flush
and segments are stitched. If the region covers every monitor there is no
room for the bar; stop via the tray icon or by re-running
.BR \-\-record .
.TP
.B \-\-pin
Capture a region and pin it to the desktop as a click-through overlay. Pins
stack and persist as long-lived processes.
.TP
.BR \-\-grab ", " \-\-release ", " \-\-close\-all
Make existing pins interactive (clickable close button + draggable), restore
them to click-through, or dismiss every pin. Intended to be wired to a
compositor hold-bind.
.TP
.B \-\-tesseract
Capture a region, OCR it via
.BR tesseract ,
and copy the text to the clipboard. Requires
.B tesseract
on
.B $PATH
plus the traineddata for the language being read
.RB ( eng
by default). When
.B ocr.tesseract
is unset, grabit probes
.B tesseract\-ocr
before
.B tesseract
on
.BR $PATH .
Set
.B ocr.lang
to OCR another language, combining several with
.RB \(dq + \(dq
.RB ( "grabit set ocr.lang eng+deu" ).
.TP
.BI \-\-translate [=lang]
With
.BR \-\-tesseract :
translate the OCR text and copy the translation instead.
.I lang
is the target language (default
.BR en ;
source auto-detected). Falls back to raw OCR if the call fails (20s cap).
.B translate.backend
picks the translator:
.B trans
(default) shells out to translate-shell's
.B trans
binary, while
.B libretranslate
POSTs to the LibreTranslate server named by
.B translate.url
.RI ( /translate
is appended if omitted), and
.B deepl
POSTs to the DeepL API using
.B translate.api_key
.RB ( GRABIT_TRANSLATE_KEY
overrides it). Neither needs an external binary. For
.BR deepl ,
the endpoint is derived from the key and
.B translate.url
overrides it. See
.B OPTIONS.md
for DeepL target codes.
.PP
Translating sends the OCR'd text to a third-party server unless you use a
self-hosted LibreTranslate instance.
.TP
.B \-\-show
With
.BR \-\-tesseract :
render the OCR/translate result on screen as a transient click-through text card
instead of copying. Auto-dismisses after
.B text_card.dismiss_secs
(default 8s).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-edit
Open the in-tree annotation editor before the action. Pairs with any action;
make it the default with
.BR "grabit set edit.default true" .
A toolbar opens at the top of the primary monitor (override with
.BR edit.toolbar_output );
drag it by its background to park it anywhere, including onto another
monitor unless
.B edit.toolbar_output
pins it to one; the parked spot is remembered across runs
.RB ( edit.toolbar_pos )
as long as that output is still connected. The editor starts in
region-select mode, but picking any tool switches to drawing immediately, so
the frozen screen can be annotated before a region exists; the select-region
button (or key
.BR q )
drags out (or replaces) the capture area, and Save stays disabled
until one is set. Tools: pen, marker, line, rect, ellipse, arrow, blur,
pixelate, spotlight, text, counter, callout, eraser (keys
.B 1\-9
or letters
.BR p / m / l / r / o / a / b / x / h / t / c / k / e ).
The spotlight tool dims everything outside the rectangle you drag, with the
width slider setting how dark the surround goes.
The callout tool draws a speech bubble: click what it should point at, type the
text, and the bubble appears offset from that spot with a tail leading back to
it; in the move/resize tool both the bubble and the tail tip are draggable.
a move/resize tool
.RB ( s )
that repositions drawn annotations (corner handles resize shapes, lines, and
arrows; strokes and text move only), an HSL color picker with eyedropper, and
a width slider (or scroll wheel; the wheel sizes text instead while the text
tool is active). Undo
.RB ( u
or
.BR Ctrl+Z ,
hold to repeat) steps back through annotations, annotation moves/resizes,
and region changes alike. Last-used color, width, and tool persist across
runs.
.SH NOTES
.SS KDE Plasma recording
KWin keeps
.B zkde_screencast_unstable_v1
on an interface blacklist and only exposes it to programs whose installed
.I .desktop
file declares
.BR X-KDE-Wayland-Interfaces=zkde_screencast_unstable_v1 .
grabit ships that key, so recording on Plasma requires an installed grabit
.RB ( make
.BR install ),
not one run from a build tree. Starting KWin with
.B KWIN_WAYLAND_NO_PERMISSION_CHECKS=1
bypasses the check for testing.
.SH MODIFIERS
.TP
.BR \-F ", " \-\-fullscreen
Capture a whole monitor instead of dragging a region. With one monitor it is
grabbed directly. With several, the selector opens dimmed and snaps to whole
monitors: hover a monitor to highlight it and click to grab it (dragging
still works for a custom region). Pairs with any capture action, including
.BR \-\-record ,
and with
.BR \-e ;
cannot be combined with
.BR \-f .
.TP
.BI \-\-fullscreen= monitor
As above, but capture a specific monitor directly (no picker).
.I monitor
is a 1-based number or an output name (e.g.
.BR \-\-fullscreen=DP\-1 ).
Use
.B \-\-fullscreen=all
to capture every monitor stitched into one image. An unknown value lists the
available monitors and exits.
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-window
Capture the focused window instead of dragging a region. Pairs with the same
actions as
.BR \-F ;
cannot be combined with
.BR \-f ,
.BR \-F ,
or
.BR \-\-record .
On Hyprland the window's geometry is read over IPC and the screen is cropped to
it, so
.B \-e
works and anything overlapping the window is included. On niri, geometry is only
published for floating windows; a floating window takes the same crop path,
while a tiled window is rendered by niri itself via its
.B screenshot\-window
action. That path needs niri 25.11 or newer, captures only the window's own
contents, cannot be annotated (grabit warns and captures without
.BR \-e ),
ignores
.B png.level
for PNG output because niri's own file is used as-is,
and, because niri always copies its window screenshots to the clipboard,
replaces the clipboard contents as a side effect. Other compositors cannot
report the active window and
.B \-w
fails there.
.TP
.BR \-L ", " \-\-last
Reuse the region from the previous capture instead of opening the selector.
The rect is recorded after every region capture and kept in the state file as
.BR region.last .
Works for screenshots and
.BR \-\-record .
With
.BR \-e
the region is applied and locked, so the editor opens on the last-used tool
rather than in region-select mode. Set
.B region.repeat_last
to
.B true
to make this the default without passing the flag.
.B \-F
takes precedence, and the flag is ignored when no region has been recorded yet.
.TP
.BI \-\-delay " secs"
Wait
.I secs
seconds before capturing, so a menu or tooltip can be opened first (0\-3600).
For screenshots the wait happens before the screen is frozen, so anything
opened during it is captured; for
.B \-\-record
it happens after the region is picked, immediately before recording starts.
Set
.B capture.delay
for a default without passing the flag.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-last
Force the region selector for this run even when
.B region.repeat_last
is
.BR true .
Overrides
.BR \-L .
.TP
.B \-\-cursor
Include the mouse pointer in the screenshot for this run even if
.B capture.cursor
is
.BR false .
The pointer is included by default; hide it with
.BR "grabit set capture.cursor false" .
.TP
.B \-\-chunked
Upload to Zipline in chunks via its partial-upload API (useful behind
Cloudflare's upload size limit). Make it permanent with
.B "grabit set services.zipline.chunked true"
and tune the chunk size (MiB) with
.BR services.zipline.chunk_size .
Plain uploads rejected with HTTP 413 (e.g. Cloudflare's 100MB cap) retry in
chunks automatically, halving the chunk size if needed. Zipline only; other
services ignore it.
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Use an existing
.I file
instead of capturing.
.TP
.BI \-\-filename " tpl"
Per-run filename template (overrides the
.B filename
config key). See
.BR "FILENAME TEMPLATES" .
.TP
.BI \-\-format " fmt"
Per-run output format:
.BR png ,
.BR jpeg ,
or
.B webp
(default
.BR png ).
JPEG/WebP must have been compiled in.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-upload
With
.BR \-\-record :
skip the auto-upload after recording even if
.BR default_action=upload .
.TP
.B \-\-no\-tray
Suppress the SNI tray icon during recording.
.TP
.BR \-\-silent ", " \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress info logging, desktop notifications, and the shutter sound (errors
still print). Failure notifications are forced and still appear.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable debug logging to standard error (same as
.BR GRABIT_DEBUG=1 ).
.TP
.B \-\-
End of options; the following argument is treated as
.BI \-f " file" .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS Configuration
Every subcommand below also accepts
.B \-\-help
.RB ( \-h )
directly, equivalent to
.BR "grabit help " subcommand .
.TP
.BI "set " "key value"
Write a config key (schema-validated). The
.BI "set " key = value
form is accepted too.
.TP
.BI "set " key
Print the example/default value for that key.
.TP
.B set
List all settable keys.
.TP
.BI "get " [key]
Print one config key, or dump every set key.
.TP
.BI "unset " key
Remove a config key.
.TP
.BI "help " [subcommand]
Print help for a subcommand
.RB ( set ,
.BR get ,
.BR unset ,
.BR sxcu ,
.BR plugin ).
.SS Custom uploaders (ShareX .sxcu)
.TP
.BI "sxcu add " file
Parse, sanitize, and register a
.B .sxcu
uploader; use it as
.BI \-\- name
(alias:
.BR install ).
.TP
.B sxcu list
Show registered uploaders (alias:
.BR ls ).
.TP
.BI "sxcu show " name
Print parsed fields.
.TP
.BI "sxcu remove " name
Remove an uploader (alias:
.BR rm ).
.SS Plugins
.TP
.BI "plugin install " git\-url
Clone, build, and install a plugin (alias:
.BR add ).
.TP
.B plugin list
List installed plugins (alias:
.BR ls ).
.TP
.BI "plugin show " name
Print the parsed manifest.
.TP
.BI "plugin update " [name]
Update one plugin, or all of them.
.TP
.BI "plugin remove " name
Uninstall a plugin (alias:
.BR rm ).
.TP
.BI name " ..."
Run the installed plugin
.BI grabit\- name
(auto-updates in the background per its manifest). With
.BI \-p " name"
the plugin's last stdout line is pinned to the desktop as a file.
Plugins with
.B capture.auto
receive a fresh screenshot path as their first argument;
.B \-\-capture
and
.B \-\-no\-capture
override that per call. See
.B PLUGINS.md
for the manifest format.
.SH FILENAME TEMPLATES
Tokens accepted by
.B \-\-filename
and the
.B filename
config key:
.TP
.B %Y %m %d %H %M %S
strftime date/time fields.
.TP
.B %s
Unix timestamp.
.TP
.BR %r [ N ]
Random alphanumeric,
.I N
characters (default 12).
.TP
.B %u
UUID v4.
.TP
.B %w
Active window class / app ID.
.TP
.B %t
Active window title.
.PP
.RB ( %w
and
.B %t
read the focused toplevel over
.BR wlr\-foreign\-toplevel\-management\-v1 ,
so they work on Hyprland, sway, niri, and river, and resolve to empty where
that protocol is missing.)
.TP
.B %%
Literal
.BR % .
.PP
Presets via the
.B filename_preset
key:
.B date
.RB ( %Y\-%m\-%d\-%H\-%M\-%S ,
default),
.B random
.RB ( %r12 ),
.B uuid
.RB ( %u ),
.B timestamp
.RB ( %s ).
.SH CONFIGURATION
The config lives at
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/grabit/config.toml
(else
.IR ~/.config/grabit/config.toml ),
written with mode 0600. Manage it with
.B grabit set/get/unset
or edit the TOML directly. Notable top-level keys:
.B default_action
.RB ( copy / upload / save / pin ),
.BR service ,
.BR notifications ,
.BR log_file ,
.BR also_save ,
.BR save_dir ,
.BR filename ,
.BR filename_preset ,
.BR format .
.B save_captures
is accepted as a legacy alias for
.BR also_save .
.B notifications
carries the same forced-failure caveat as
.BR \-\-silent .
Per-service auth tokens go under
.BI services. name .auth
or, preferred, the
.BI GRABIT_ SERVICE _AUTH
environment variable.
.PP
Other service keys:
.B services.zipline.domain
(zipline endpoint; required for zipline uploads,
.B /api/upload
is appended when missing),
.BI services.zipline.headers. name
(zipline upload metadata; twelve validated header keys, see
.BR OPTIONS.md ),
and
.B services.nest.folder
(target folder for nest uploads).
.PP
See
.B OPTIONS.md
for the full key reference, including region snap/confirm, keybinds, encoder
quality, recording, sound, pin, translate, preview/text card, and edit defaults.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GRABIT_DEBUG
If set to
.BR 1 ,
enable debug logging (same as
.BR \-d ).
.TP
.BI GRABIT_ SERVICE _AUTH
Per-service auth token, overriding config.
.I SERVICE
is one of
.BR ZIPLINE ,
.BR NEST ,
.BR FAKECRIME ,
.BR EZ ,
.BR GUNS ,
.BR PIXELVAULT .
.TP
.B GRABIT_BIN
Set by plugin dispatch; absolute path to the grabit binary.
.TP
.BR GRABIT_PLUGIN_NAME ", " GRABIT_PLUGIN_DIR ", " GRABIT_CACHE_DIR
Also set by plugin dispatch: the plugin's name, install directory, and
per-plugin cache directory. See
.BR PLUGINS.md .
.TP
.B png.level
PNG zlib compression, 0\-9, default
.BR 1 .
PNG is lossless, so this trades encode time against file size only. Level 6 (the
old behaviour) costs roughly 2\-6x the encode time of level 1 for about 15\-20%
less size, and dominates the wall time of a screenshot.
.TP
.B GRABIT_LOG_FILE
Set to
.B 0
to disable the log file and log to stderr only; any other value forces it on.
Takes precedence over the
.B log_file
config key.
.TP
.B GRABIT_CAPTURE_BACKEND
Force the capture backend:
.BR auto ,
.BR wlr ,
.BR ext ,
or
.BR kwin .
Takes precedence over the
.B capture.backend
config key.
.TP
.B GRABIT_CLIPBOARD_BACKEND
Force the clipboard protocol:
.BR auto ,
.BR ext ,
or
.BR wlr .
.B auto
prefers
.B ext_data_control_v1
and falls back to the deprecated
.BR zwlr_data_control_v1 .
.TP
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
Wayland socket to connect to. Named in the connection-failure message when
grabit cannot reach a compositor.
.TP
.B HOME
Required when
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is unset: grabit exits with
.RB \(dq "HOME is not set" \(dq
if neither is present. Also backs the
.IR ~/Pictures ,
.IR ~/Videos ,
and
.I ~/.cache
fallbacks.
.TP
.B HYPRLAND_INSTANCE_SIGNATURE
Set by Hyprland; with
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
it locates the Hyprland IPC socket that powers window snapping and
.BR \-w / \-\-window .
.TP
.B NIRI_SOCKET
Set by niri; locates the niri IPC socket that powers
.BR \-w / \-\-window
and window snapping. Absent elsewhere, both degrade gracefully.
.TP
.BR XCURSOR_THEME ", " XCURSOR_SIZE
Cursor theme and size for the region selector and overlays
.RI ( XCURSOR_SIZE
is clamped to 8..256, default 24).
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Holds the recording pid file and per-pin IPC sockets (falls back to
.IR /tmp ).
.TP
.B XDG_PICTURES_DIR
Screenshot save dir. The
.B save_dir
config key takes precedence; otherwise this, else
.IR ~/Pictures .
.TP
.B XDG_VIDEOS_DIR
Recording save directory. The
.B save_dir
config key takes precedence; otherwise this variable is used, falling back to
.IR ~/Videos .
Screenshots use
.B save_dir
else
.IR ~/Pictures .
.TP
.B TESSDATA_PREFIX
Tesseract language-data directory.
.TP
.B GRABIT_TRANSLATE_KEY
API key for the
.B deepl
and
.B libretranslate
backends, overriding the
.B translate.api_key
config key.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to any value, disable ANSI color in log output.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/grabit/config.toml
User configuration (TOML), mode 0600. Only ever written by
.BR "grabit set" / unset .
It may hold upload tokens under
.BR services. \fIname\fB .auth ,
so use the
.B GRABIT_ \fISERVICE\fB _AUTH
environment variables instead if you track it in version control.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/grabit/state.toml
Machine-local state grabit writes on its own: the last-used
.BR edit.color ", " edit.width ", " edit.tool
and the editor toolbar position
.RB ( edit.toolbar_pos ).
Falls back to
.IR ~/.local/state/grabit/state.toml .
These override the matching
.B edit.*
keys in config.toml, which then act only as an initial value.
.TP
.I ~/.config/grabit/uploaders/<name>.sxcu
Registered ShareX uploaders.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/grabit.log
Every message grabit emits, with a timestamp and pid, including info and debug
lines. Falls back to
.IR /tmp/grabit- uid .log .
Notifications that say
.B check the log file
mean this one, since grabit is usually run from a keybind with no terminal
attached. That line is added only while the log file is enabled. It is
truncated once it grows past 1 MiB. On by default; turn it off
with
.B grabit set log_file false
or
.BR GRABIT_LOG_FILE=0 .
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/grabit-show.pid
PID file for the on-screen text/preview card.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/grabit_recording.pid
PID file for the active recording (falls back to
.IR /tmp/grabit_recording.pid ).
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/grabit/
Temporary captures for the clipboard and upload flows, removed after use
(falls back to
.IR /tmp ).
.TP
.I ~/.config/grabit/plugins/<name>/
Installed plugins (binaries symlinked from
.IR plugins/.bin/ ;
per-plugin cache under
.IR ~/.cache/grabit/plugins/<name>/ ).
Plugin bookkeeping lives alongside them:
.I plugins/.lock
(install/update lock) and per-plugin
.IR .source ,
.IR .last_check ,
.I .update.log
files.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B grabit \-c
Region screenshot to the clipboard.
.TP
.B grabit \-u
Upload using the
.B service
config key.
.TP
.B grabit \-\-zipline
Upload to a specific service.
.TP
.B grabit \-o > shot.txt
Save and capture the path.
.TP
.B grabit \-F \-o
Save a whole-monitor screenshot.
.TP
.B grabit \-\-fullscreen=DP\-1 \-c
Copy monitor DP-1 to the clipboard.
.TP
.B grabit \-e \-u
Annotate, then upload.
.TP
.B grabit \-\-record
Start recording (re-run to stop).
.TP
.B grabit \-\-pin
Pin a region to the desktop.
.TP
.B grabit \-f shot.png \-\-zipline
Upload an existing file.
.TP
.B grabit \-\-tesseract \-\-translate=ja
OCR a region and copy the Japanese translation.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime failure (capture, upload, clipboard, plugin, or subcommand error).
Cancelling an interactive selection also exits
.BR 1 ,
but without an error notification.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line parse or usage error.
